Z||000000||qwikgta||04-27-2001||05:59 PM||||A while back I ordered a set of KYB Front/Rear struts/shocks from the Fiero Store.  They list the rear part as fitting the 84-88 with the same part number (57606).  I just went out this afternoon and looked at the rear of my 88 coupe and the struts look diff. The ones in the box look just like the ones on my 87 coupe.  It looks to me that the spring pocket is diff on the 87 vs 88.  The 87 is little on bottom gets bigger going up/ 88 same size all the way up.  I was not able to reach the Fiero Shop cause it was after hours so my question is did I get the correct part.  Are the Rear struts diff on the 88 vs the 84-87 cars.  Common sence tells me yes but again in the fireo store catolog under the KYB/Koni/Monroe its listed as fitting the 84-88.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||gixxer||04-27-2001||07:20 PM||||A stock '88 Formula Fiero rear spring is ~5.5" center of the wire to center on all the coils except the bottom coil, which is ~4.12".<BR>I know that 'cause I just measured it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||04-27-2001||08:06 PM||||dono why that would be since 88 struts are very different <P><BR>Oh duh it's the top mount plate thats different sometimes I amaze myself with stupidity  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||5
